<title>GERMANY: Deutsche -Report on AGF buy is &quot;pure speculation&quot;.</title>
<headline>Deutsche -Report on AGF buy is &quot;pure speculation&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deutsche Bank AG on Wednesday dismissed as &quot;pure speculation&quot; a newspaper report that it wanted to take over French insurance group Assurances Generales de France (AGF).</p>
<p>&quot;That is pure speculation,&quot; a Deutsche spokesman said in response to a Reuters enquiry.</p>
<p>German daily Die Welt reported in its Wednesday edition that Deutsche wanted to take over a leading French insurer and cited unnamed industry watchers as saying it was targeting AGF.</p>
<p>Deutsche chief executive Rolf Breuer said last month his bank was mulling an acquisition in the French financial services sector.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
